---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { githubUrl, sourceZipUrl } from '../../lib/config';
const commands = [
 {title:'Clone the project',id:'clone',command:'git clone https://github.com/AlanDarfin/DarfinOS.git\ncd DarfinOS',info:'Start from the public source and review what you plan to run.'},
 {title:'Doctor & preflight',id:'doctor',command:'python3 DarfinOSInstallScript-TUI.py --doctor\nbash DarfinOSInstallScript.sh --preflight',info:'Validate the installer structure and basic system requirements. No sudo, installation or updates.'},
 {title:'Check installed modules',id:'modules',command:'python3 DarfinOSInstallScript-TUI.py --check-modules\nbash DarfinOSInstallScript.sh --check-modules',info:'Shows complete, partial, missing and unknown modules. Only verified complete steps are skipped automatically.'},
 {title:'Choose a preset without executing it',id:'presets',command:'python3 DarfinOSInstallScript-TUI.py --list-presets\npython3 DarfinOSInstallScript-TUI.py --plan --preset minimal\npython3 DarfinOSInstallScript-TUI.py --plan --preset retro',info:'Six presets are available: minimal, desktop, i3, retro, workstation, gaming and full. Full includes high-risk changes, but excludes optional Labs modules.'},
 {title:'Audit packages and compare presets',id:'audit',command:'python3 DarfinOSInstallScript-TUI.py --audit --preset gaming\npython3 DarfinOSInstallScript-TUI.py --compare-presets minimal gaming',info:'Read-only previews. Package inventory is partial and is not proof that a module is configured.'},
 {title:'Explore DarfinOS Labs',id:'labs',command:'bash DarfinOSInstallScript.sh --labs\npython3 DarfinOSInstallScript-TUI.py --lab-info chicago95',info:'Discover 28 independent projects, original upstream links and safety categories.'},
 {title:'Back up selected configuration',id:'backup',command:'python3 darfinos_control.py backup ~/darfinos-config.zip\npython3 darfinos_control.py restore ~/darfinos-config.zip',info:'Selected HOME files only. The restore command without --apply is a preview, not a system snapshot.'},
];
---
<Base title="Documentation · DarfinOS" description="English DarfinOS documentation: installation, safe preflight, module checks, profiles, Labs, maintenance and recovery.">
  <section class="grid-bg border-b border-white/10">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 py-16 md:py-20">
      <p class="section-kicker mb-4">// INSTALLATION & REFERENCE</p>
      <h1 class="section-heading">Your Arch, <span class="text-electric">my rules.</span></h1>
      <p class="section-lead mt-5 max-w-3xl">The safe way to explore an opinionated Arch Linux post-install toolkit. Nothing here requires you to run random remote scripts as root.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-8">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={sourceZipUrl}>Download current source ZIP</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/downloads/">Downloads & release status</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href={githubUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source code ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 py-14">
    <nav aria-label="Guide sections" class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-11 text-sm">
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="#requirements">Requirements</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="#commands">Commands</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="#tui">TUI</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="#safety">Safety</a>
    </nav>

    <section id="requirements" class="card doc-card">
      <p class="section-kicker">01 / REQUIREMENTS</p>
      <h2>Start with a working Arch installation.</h2>
      <p>DarfinOS is not a Linux distribution, bootable installer or ISO. It is a modular post-install customization project for Arch Linux and compatible pacman-based systems.</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-300 space-y-2 mt-4">
        <li>Arch Linux or a compatible system with <code>pacman</code>.</li>
        <li>Normal user account with <code>sudo</code> for installation stages.</li>
        <li>Python 3 with <code>curses</code> for the TUI. No pip installation is required.</li>
        <li>A recovery plan and preferably a snapshot before touching XLibre, SonicDE, Bedrock or boot components.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="commands" class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mt-6">
      {commands.map(item => <article class="card" id={item.id}>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">{item.title}</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">{item.info}</p>
        <div class="code-panel"><pre><code>{item.command}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy={item.command} aria-label={'Copy commands: ' + item.title}>Copy</button></div>
      </article>)}
    </section>

    <section id="tui" class="card doc-card mt-6">
      <p class="section-kicker">02 / THE TERMINAL UI</p>
      <h2>Plan first, install second.</h2>
      <p>Launch <code>python3 DarfinOSInstallScript-TUI.py --local</code>. Opening the TUI does not start installing. Use the arrow keys to navigate, Space to select, <code>/</code> to search, and <code>R</code> to review before execution.</p>
      <p>For an interface preview, use <code>python3 DarfinOSInstallScript-TUI.py --local --dry-run</code>. This keeps execution in simulation mode while you explore its menus.</p>
      <p>Useful keys: <strong>I</strong> refreshes module detection, <strong>X</strong> toggles explicit re-execution, <strong>L</strong> browses Labs, <strong>O</strong> opens presets, <strong>C</strong> shows system status, and <strong>V</strong> opens a partial package audit.</p>
      <p>To rerun a stage from Bash, use <code>--only i3 --reinstall</code>. This does not bypass pacman's <code>--needed</code>, project-specific confirmations or overwrite protection.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="safety" class="card doc-card mt-6">
      <p class="section-kicker">03 / LIMITS</p>
      <h2>Know what the software does not prove.</h2>
      <p>A package being installed does not mean an entire desktop, login manager or service is configured. DarfinOS automatically skips only steps for which it can verify enough evidence. Others remain partial or unknown.</p>
      <p>Chicago95 is downloaded from the <a href="https://github.com/grassmunk/Chicago95" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">original project</a>; the optional Retro stage copies GTK/Xfwm themes, icons, cursors and fonts without executing its remote Python installer or changing your current Xfce settings.</p>
      <p>There is currently <strong>no stable release</strong>. CI validates offline behavior and a safe Arch container, not a complete graphical VM installation or restore workflow.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-6"><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/controle/">Control Center ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/labs/">All Labs projects ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/downloads/">Release status ↗</a></div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <p id="copy-status" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const value = button.dataset.copy;
      if (!value) return;
      try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(value); button.textContent = 'Copied!'; }
      catch { button.textContent = 'Select the text'; }
    }));
  </script>
</Base>
